# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets
#
# The allow-list form on purpose: `.env.*` catches `.env.production`,
# `.env.render`, `.env.backup` and every other variant someone invents at 2am,
# and the two `!` lines put back the only files that are meant to be public.
# Listing individual names would mean the next variant is the one that leaks.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example
*.key
*.pem

# Data / artifacts
data/
outputs/
out/

# The sidecars matter as much as the database. `*.db` does NOT match
# `jobtailor.db-wal`, and the write-ahead log holds recent transactions — which
# here means the full text of whatever resume was last parsed. Both files sit
# next to the database on any machine that has run the app.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Run artifacts. These hold the full text of whatever resume was parsed —
# a name, an address, a phone number, an employment history. v1 kept exactly
# this kind of folder at the repo root WITHOUT ignoring it, so real resume
# PDFs were one `git add -A` from being public.
runs/

# Cached stage results. A cached parse is the full text of a resume, so this
# is personal data for the same reason runs/ is.
.cache/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
out/

# Tooling
.import_linter_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
